# What must NOT go into the .vsix.
#
# vsce's own default is "everything in this directory except node_modules
# devDependencies", which is wrong here in one specific way: `demo/` is a
# Delphi project kept for driving the client BY HAND, and running it leaves a
# `pastree-lsp.log` next to the .dproj (that is where the server writes its
# log - see the repo's CLAUDE.md). So the packaged extension was carrying a
# 180-200 KB log of somebody's last debugging session, growing with every run,
# for no reason at all: an installed extension has nothing to do with a demo
# project on the packager's disk.
#
# Not a blanket "ignore junk" list - each line says what would otherwise ship.

# The manual-test project, and the server log it produces.
demo/**

# The lockfile pins what to INSTALL, not what to run; the resolved tree is
# already in the package.
package-lock.json

# Previously built packages, when one is built in place.
*.vsix
